common-passwords-12plus.txt.gz
================================

Used only to reject common passwords at registration, reset and change (docs/SECURITY.md §1, S1 decision D-3).
It contains passwords only (no usernames, emails or other identifiers).

Source: "xato-net-10-million-passwords-1000000.txt" from SecLists
  https://github.com/danielmiessler/SecLists/tree/master/Passwords/Common-Credentials
  SecLists licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2018 Daniel Miessler.

Underlying data: Mark Burnett's "ten million passwords" set (xato.net, February 2015), which its author
stated he was "releasing to the public domain".

Processing (2026-11-09): Unicode NFKC, case-folded, kept entries of 12 to 256 characters (shorter ones
are already rejected by the 12-character minimum), dropped lines with undecodable bytes, de-duplicated,
sorted, gzip. 46,146 entries.
